/* loading_overlay — daisyUI skin (residual).
 *
 * Everything this component needs is in the examples' markup except one rule, which cannot be
 * spelled as a class: an *empty* overlay draws its spinner with a `::before`, and that spinner is
 * a daisyUI component class. A pseudo-element cannot be given a class, and `d-loading`'s value is
 * a percent-encoded SVG mask with a `prefers-reduced-motion` variant behind it — inlining that as
 * an arbitrary utility would be unreadable in an example and would not survive a daisyUI upgrade.
 * So this one rule stays, and only this one.
 */
.chelekom-loading-overlay:not(:has(> *)):before {
  @apply <%= @d %>loading <%= @d %>loading-spinner;

  content: "";
}
